  "findings": [
    "All three ordinary elementary/Troe/PLOG full summaries pass, and lowercase ea retains the required Ea YAML refusal.",
    "Eight unsupported-model-key expectations fail: each process exits zero without stderr and emits a summary identical to its corresponding positive witness.",
    "Uppercase B=1 is accepted while the observed temperature exponent remains zero, demonstrating the default b=0 rather than requested exponent.",
    "Nested units, orders and negative-A assertions are admitted without the required unsupported-key refusal; summaries do not reflect these added keys.",
    "Lowercase t2 is accepted. Inspect summaries do not expose Troe T2, so the value loss is inferred from exact RawTroe source (unknown key ignored, optional T2 absent), not directly measured rate behavior."
  ],
  "repair_implications": [
    "Prioritize a narrow separate nested modeled-key admission lane: RawRate must capture and refuse unknowns across ordinary and high/low-pressure blocks; RawTroe must independently capture and refuse unknowns.",
    "RawPressureRate flattens RawRate. A naive deny_unknown_fields or competing flattened maps risks rejecting modeled P or swallowing entry extras; require an explicit tested P/A/b/Ea key boundary or suitable private visitor while preserving existing typed paths and required-field behavior.",
    "Preserve b=0 default when genuinely omitted, optional T2 when genuinely omitted, required A/Ea/P/Troe parameters, numeric/quoted/nonfinite semantics, duplicate-key refusals, units normalization, and the separate six annotation allowlists.",
    "Freeze separately bound repaired-source evidence; preserve these first outcomes and run original fifty, supplement twenty with its historical failures, prior fifteen CLI controls, affected libraries and candidate-associated policy/CI gates before integration."
  ],
